a Florida college student is in custody  after a security breach at a Florida  Airport 22 year-old Michelle Sanket is  charged with criminal attempt to steal a  plane yesterday at Orlando Melbourne  International Airport only the co poll  shows us how the potentially dangerous  situation was diffused by fast-acting  employees Toni good morning good morning  Sankat was a part-time student at  Florida Institute of Technology he was  studying aviation management now  according to the FAA he had received a  commercial pilot's license back in  January but besides being 22 and a  student he was not qualified to fly this  type of plane there obviously seem to be  some planning involved police in Florida  are trying to determine what 22 year old  Kneeshaw Sankat was planning to do after  he boarded a commercial airliner  undergoing maintenance early Thursday  morning if he was a student pilot from  the area he would be familiar with the  airfield  authorities say the student pilot drove  to the curb outside the airport around  2:00 a.m. and left his car running he  then hopped a barbed wire fence and  boarded an American Airlines plane  sitting near a hangar the individual was  confronted as soon as he was on the  aircraft the employee who was on that  aircraft actually took the appropriate  action and escorted him off of the  aircraft but after he was dragged from  the plane he broke free running back  toward the jet soon after police took  him into custody within two minutes of  creating a problem we stopped this guy  from getting in the air this is only the  latest security breach involving a  commercial airliner last month a luggage  handler died after taking control of an  empty jet at seattle-tacoma  International Airport he conducted a  number of dangerous maneuvers before  crashing sand cat from the republic of  trinidad and tobago was studying in  florida on a visa he was not armed at  the time but police searched his car for  explosives before towing it away we're  obviously going to review all all of our  security you can rest assured that we  believe that in this instance our  security worked just fine police say  they searched San cats home and  confiscated his electronics but at this  time authorities say there is no  evidence to indicate a connection to  terrorism biana Tony thank you
 

